863 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 409 0 R/T(Intake/Transfer Overview)/E(Intake/Transfer Overview)/Pg 17 0 R/K[65]>>
endobj

864 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 409 0 R/E(For this season\220s intake, we prioritized a touch-it-own-it style design, with efficiency and speed as our primary goals. After more than eight total iterations and refinements, we finalized our V3 intake, which has proven to be highly reliable and effective. The intake spans the full width of the robot and uses vectored wheels on both sides to guide artifacts smoothly toward the center. Running at approximately 2,000 RPM, it allows for near-instant artifact intake. The first three intake stages are powered, while the transfer system is powered by separate motor. The transfer system consists of three stages, including a back roller, all operating at 2,500 RPM, enabling consistent and rapid firing. Through extensive iteration and testing, this design has shown strong performance and reliability, and we have not encountered issues since finalizing it.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[66]>>
endobj

