<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 412 0 R/T(ARC-CV)/E(ARC-CV)/Pg 20 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

989 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 412 0 R/T(Team Created CameraVision Method)/E(Team Created CameraVision Method)/Pg 20 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

990 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 412 0 R/T(This year, recognizing camera vision's critical role in the DECODE season, our team leveraged online FTC resources to integrate it into our codebase. We evaluated multiple vision libraries, but encountered unreliable pose estimates and inconsistent AprilTag detection under variable lighting. After in-depth research into FTC VisionPortal capabilities, we developed ARC-CV \(Autonomous Range & Curve Computer Vision\), our custom vision layer built atop the official SDK. ARC-CV provides driver-assist aiming by processing AprilTag detections to estimate robot pose relative to scoring targets, while analyzing simulated ball trajectories to compute path errors. It factors in detection confidence alongside horizontal/vertical miss distances, feeding these metrics into real-time adjustments for our shooter's angle and velocity equations. All telemetry overlays are clearly marked as prototype/simulated during development.)/E(This year, recognizing camera vision's critical role in the DECODE season, our team leveraged online FTC resources to integrate it into our codebase. We evaluated multiple vision libraries, but encountered unreliable pose estimates and inconsistent AprilTag detection under variable lighting. After in-depth research into FTC VisionPortal capabilities, we developed ARC-CV \(Autonomous Range & Curve Computer Vision\), our custom vision layer built atop the official SDK. ARC-CV provides driver-assist aiming by processing AprilTag detections to estimate robot pose relative to scoring targets, while analyzing simulated ball trajectories to compute path errors. It factors in detection confidence alongside horizontal/vertical miss distances, feeding these metrics into real-time adjustments for our shooter's angle and velocity equations. All telemetry overlays are clearly marked as prototype/simulated during development.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

991 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 412 0 R/T(Translational Velocity Adjustment Deriving Equations)/E(Translational Velocity Adjustment Deriving Equations)/Pg 20 0 R/K[3]>>
