<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 413 0 R/T(To start, we take a picture with our LimeLight 3A camera. With this image, we create a color mask in a region of interest. We also use morphology functions to reduce noise and focus only on specific desired artifacts.)/E(To start, we take a picture with our LimeLight 3A camera. With this image, we create a color mask in a region of interest. We also use morphology functions to reduce noise and focus only on specific desired artifacts.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

1031 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 413 0 R/E(Next, we apply canny edge detection and contour detection to generate bounding boxes around individual artifacts, separating them even when they appear clustered together.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

1032 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 413 0 R/T(Next, we perform a homography transformation to obtain real world coordinates and angle by mapping the real world points onto pixel coordinates.)/E(Next, we perform a homography transformation to obtain real world coordinates and angle by mapping the real world points onto pixel coordinates.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

1033 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 413 0 R/E(Next, for each artifact, we draw rectangles along the perpendicular bisector of the artifact and check whether they intersect any artifacts; if so, that artifact is removed from our candidate list.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

1034 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 413 0 R/T(For each artifact, we draw a circle centered at the intake that just contacts the ball, then construct a tangent at that point. We then select the ball whose tangent direction requires the least physical rotation.)/E(For each artifact, we draw a circle centered at the intake that just contacts the ball, then construct a tangent at that point. We then select the ball whose tangent direction requires the least physical rotation.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[26]>>
endobj

1035 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/P 413 0 R/T(Using the real-world coordinates of the chosen ball, we position the drivetrain and turret 2 inches offset from its perpendicular bisector. Then we drive forward, using our intake and robot position, until the infrared sensor detects the ball.)/E(Using the real-world coordinates of the chosen ball, we position the drivetrain and turret 2 inches offset from its perpendicular bisector. Then we drive forward, using our intake and robot position, until the infrared sensor detects the ball.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[27]>>
endobj

1036 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 413 0 R/E(Throughout early DECODE events, our team used a simpler vision pipeline that detected a blob of balls using contour detection and just drove our intake into the blob. This approach was very ineffective, which pushed us to redesign for later events.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[28]>>
endobj

