2481 0 obj
<</Title(This year, recognizing camera vision's critical role in the DECODE season, our team leveraged online FTC resources to integrate it into our codebase. We evaluated multiple vision libraries, but encountered unreliable pose estimates and inconsistent AprilTag detection under variable lighting. After in-depth research into FTC VisionPortal capabilities, we developed ARC-CV \(Autonomous Range & Curve Computer Vision\), our custom vision layer built atop the official SDK. ARC-CV provides driver-assist aiming by processing AprilTag detections to estimate robot pose relative to scoring targets, while analyzing simulated ball trajectories to compute path errors. It factors in detection confidence alongside horizontal/vertical miss distances, feeding these metrics into real-time adjustments for our shooter's angle and velocity equations. All telemetry overlays are clearly marked as prototype/simulated during development.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2456 0 R>>
endobj

2482 0 obj
<</Title(Our localization evolved from two-wheel odometry \(parallel + perpendicular dead wheels, Control Hub IMU heading\) to three-wheel \(two parallel + one perpendicular pod\) for direct heading calculation and less drift. Encoder slot limits led us to the goBILDA Pinpoint computer.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2457 0 R/Next 2506 0 R>>
endobj

2483 0 obj
<</Title(After deployment, we stress tested ARC-CV under varied lighting and field layouts to improve consistency. We optimized filtering, reduced latency, and fused tag pose data with odometry for precise autonomous alignment.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2457 0 R/Prev 2506 0 R>>
endobj

